BT\n/F1 8 Tf\n50 750 Td\n(TextFix - Research Correction Report
Ethiopian New Curriculum - Grade 11 Biology
Unit 1: Biology and Technology \\(Pages 1-20\\)
------------------------------------------------------------------------
Verification Philosophy: Evidence-Based, Human-Verified
Contact: info.textfix@gmail.com

PAGE 1 \\(Cover\\)
No errors found. Verified clean.

PAGE 2
P2-01 | Grammar
Original: "Organisms have well-adapted structures and that make them survive on their immediate environment."
Issue: Redundant "and" before "that"; wrong preposition \\("on" instead of "in"\\).
Correction: "Organisms have well-adapted structures that help them survive in their immediate environment."

P2-02 | Grammar
Original: "The better their understanding the diverse nature of biological materials, the better their ability to develop technologies."
Issue: Missing "of" after "understanding."
Correction: "The better their understanding of the diverse nature of biological materials, the better their ability to develop technologies."

P2-03 | Conceptual / Definitional
Original: "Nature is the physical, natural and material world of life that exists without human intervention..."
Issue: Nature defined as "world of life," but following examples are mostly non-living.
Correction: "Nature is the physical and material world that exists without human intervention."

P2-04 | Word Choice
Original: "Nature provides us with doable structures and forms..."
Issue: "Doable" describes tasks, not structures/forms.
Correction: "Nature provides us with usable structures and forms..."

P2-05 | Word Choice
Original: "...they can sketch the biological structures, design functional mechanisms and tune into more efficient technologies..."
Issue: "Tune into" does not fit here.
Correction: "...design functional mechanisms, and turn them into more efficient technologies..."

PAGE 3
P3-01 | Grammar
Original: "The design and adaptation of many technologies we utilize today imitated natural working systems."
Issue: Broken sentence structure/verb tense.
Correction: "Many of the technologies we use today were designed and adapted by imitating natural working systems."

P3-02 | Word Choice / Grammar
Original: "Many technologies have been imitating birds, bats, termites, spiders, bees, ants and parts of human body since timeless."
Issue: Wrong voice; missing article; "since timeless" is non-standard.
Correction: "Many technologies have imitated birds, bats, termites, spiders, bees, ants, and parts of the human body since time immemorial."

P3-03 | Factual Error \\(Pairs with P4-01\\)
Original: "An example is The East gate Center in Harare \\(Figure 1.2\\)."
Issue: Building's actual name is Eastgate Centre. Caption on next page calls it "East Gate Building".
Correction: "An example is the Eastgate Centre in Harare \\(Figure 1.2\\)."

PAGE 4
P4-01 | Consistency \\(Pairs with P3-03\\)
Caption: "Mound inspired architecture for the East Gate Building" -> "Mound-inspired architecture for the Eastgate Centre"

P4-02 | Punctuation
Missing terminal period at end of item 4.

P4-03 | Grammar
Original: "Engineers imitating human eyes made the technology of photograph camera."
Correction: "Engineers imitating the human eye developed camera technology."

P4-04 | Grammar
Original: "The movement of bio-robots was designed from the movement of kangaroo."
Correction: "The movement of bio-robots was designed from the movement of kangaroos."

P4-05 | Consistency / Article
Original: "Injection needle technology was copied from mosquito proboscis \\(Figure 1.3\\)."
Correction: "Injection needle technology was copied from a mosquito's proboscis \\(Figure 1.3\\)."

P4-06 | Scientific Terminology
Original: "Synthetic bulletproof vests are imitations of the spin silks of spiders."
Correction: "Synthetic bulletproof vests are imitations of spider silk."

P4-07 | Scientific Terminology \\(Needs Expert Review\\)
Original: "Ceramics are an imitation of the nature of crack-resistant shellfish exoskeleton."
Issue: Mollusk shells are usually called shells, not exoskeletons. Flagged for biology expert review.
Correction: "Ceramics are an imitation of the crack-resistant shell structure of shellfish \\(nacre\\)."

PAGE 5
P5-01 | Consistency
Caption: "Robotic arms imitated from elephant trunk" -> "Robotic arm imitated from an elephant's trunk"

P5-02 | Typo
"How closely does your model hand match a natural human hand?'" -> remove stray apostrophe.

PAGE 6
P6-01 | Consistency \\(Layout Check\\)
Margin question duplicate variants: "coupling" vs "blend". Unify to "blend".

P6-02 | Typo
"...artificial versions of the these biochemical substances." -> remove duplicate article.

P6-03 | Consistency \\(See also P17-04\\)
Technology defined three different ways across the unit. Canonical definition recommended.

PAGE 7
P7-01 | Consistency
"A brand new drone design" -> "Drone design" \\(parallel noun-phrase style\\).

PAGE 8
P8-01 | Formatting
"1.2.2Uses of technology in biology" -> add space: "1.2.2 Uses of technology in biology"

P8-02 | Grammar
"Biomedical studies deal with providing detailed of information..." -> "detailed information"

P8-03 | Conceptual / Category Error
"Biogeographical information is the study of..." -> "Biogeography is the study of..."

P8-04 | Formatting \\(List Numbering\\)
Missing number between 1 \\(thermometer\\) and 2 \\(blood test\\). Renumber pregnancy test "2." and resume sequentially.

P8-05 | Grammar
"...confirms the existence pregnancy..." -> "existence of pregnancy"

PAGE 9
P9-01 | Typo
"taking sample blood from figure tip" -> "from the fingertip"

P9-02 | Recurring Layout Error
Running header reads "UNIT 2: ANIMALS" across pages 9, 11, 13, 15, 17, and 19 in Unit 1!
Correction: Change running header to "UNIT 1: BIOLOGY AND TECHNOLOGY".

PAGE 10
P10-01 | Flag for Expert Verification
"Computer Information Technology Scanning \\(CITS\\)" is not recognized in medical literature.
Flagged for expert verification to confirm intended modality or cut.

P10-02 | Factual Error
"Geographical Position System \\(GPS\\)" -> "Global Positioning System \\(GPS\\)"
